.TH WMVOL 1 "2026" "wmvol 1.0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wmvol \- Window Maker PipeWire volume dockapp
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wmvol
[\fB\-display\fR \fIDPY\fR] [\fB\-w\fR] [\fB\-s\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-l\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-m\fR \fICMD\fR] [\fB\-f\fR \fIFONT\fR] [\fB\-fg\fR \fIRRGGBB\fR] [\fB\-D\fR \fIPREFIX\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
A 64x64 Window Maker dockapp showing the default PipeWire output volume. Left click opens a popup mixer
with output/input volume, mute and default-device selection. Uses \fBwpctl\fR(1); updates instantly if
\fBpactl\fR(1) is installed.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-display DPY
X display to use.
.TP
.B \-w
Run in a normal window instead of docking.
.TP
.B \-s N
Wheel step in percent, 1\-100 (default 5).
.TP
.B \-l N
Volume limit in percent, 10\-200 (default 100).
.TP
.B \-m CMD
Command for "Open full mixer" (default pavucontrol).
.TP
.B \-f FONT
Popup font as an Xft pattern (default sans-10).
.TP
.B \-fg RRGGBB
LCD colour (default 20b2aa).
.TP
.B \-D PREFIX
Debug: write PREFIX\-tile.ppm and PREFIX\-popup.ppm and exit.
.SH MOUSE
Tile: left click popup; wheel output volume (shift: 1%); middle click mute; right click next output;
ctrl+wheel / ctrl+middle input volume / mute; ctrl+right click open mixer.
Popup: click icon to mute, drag slider, click a device to make it default, Esc or click outside to close.
Hold the Window Maker modifier (usually Alt) and drag to move the tile in the dock.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wpctl (1),
.BR wmaker (1)
